1
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,891
Here is Revoke Line's recorded incident response on Flux Nova.

2
00:00:06,891 --> 00:00:10,214
An authorized case initially receives HTTP two hundred, allow.

3
00:00:10,214 --> 00:00:15,012
A simulated provider security alert then revokes trust and increments the provider version.

4
00:00:15,012 --> 00:00:19,811
When the workflow attempts to use its old grant, the gateway returns HTTP

5
00:00:19,811 --> 00:00:24,610
four oh three, deny. The worker routes the case to a native human

6
00:00:24,610 --> 00:00:27,932
review task in the B P M N engine.

7
00:00:27,932 --> 00:00:32,731
This is an actual engine task, not just a status displayed in the

8
00:00:32,731 --> 00:00:33,100
interface.

9
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:36,793
The second recorded scenario tests selective containment.

10
00:00:36,793 --> 00:00:39,445
Two independent providers are initially authorized.

11
00:00:39,445 --> 00:00:45,189
Only provider A is revoked. Its next call is denied and its workflow

12
00:00:45,189 --> 00:00:49,608
enters human review. Provider B remains authorized and completes normally.

13
00:00:49,608 --> 00:00:55,353
We verified its automated end event through Flux Nova process and activity history,

14
00:00:55,353 --> 00:00:58,888
not simply the disappearance of an active instance.

15
00:00:58,888 --> 00:01:04,633
The result demonstrates targeted containment in this two-case scenario, without unnecessarily interrupting the

16
00:01:04,633 --> 00:01:05,517
unaffected workflow.

17
00:01:06,117 --> 00:01:09,495
The third scenario tests a real service outage.

18
00:01:09,495 --> 00:01:14,985
With the same healthy provider and valid grant, the initial request is allowed.

19
00:01:14,985 --> 00:01:20,475
We stop the local Flux Nova container, and the next request returns HTTP

20
00:01:20,475 --> 00:01:25,965
five oh three, deny. After restart, the script waits for the same pinned

21
00:01:25,965 --> 00:01:28,499
policy to become available. Authorization resumes.

22
00:01:28,499 --> 00:01:31,455
Both workflow and decision services were interrupted.

23
00:01:31,455 --> 00:01:36,100
The result demonstrates fail-closed authorization and recovery, not continuous workflow availability.

24
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:40,874
The assurance view recalculates checks against saved integration evidence.

25
00:01:40,874 --> 00:01:46,902
All three recorded scenarios pass. Sixty-eight automated regression tests pass, all sixteen decision

26
00:01:46,902 --> 00:01:52,931
combinations were verified on the live engine, and strict CALM validation reports no

27
00:01:52,931 --> 00:01:58,959
errors or warnings. Production readiness is deliberately blocked because important controls remain incomplete.

28
00:01:58,959 --> 00:02:04,524
These are verifiable prototype results, with explicit boundaries, not a compliance certification.

29
